{"posts":[{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1151","t":"We must always keep in mind that \"We look for QMs at HTF Supply and Demand.\" as IF wrote in the first line of the first post of this thread.","a":"Al3cs","d":"","n":"#1151","p":47,"im":[],"m":1151},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1152","t":"another Qt QM\n\nGUNNER","a":"pmbGUNNER","d":"","n":"#1152","p":47,"im":["b0472a8dc1e5a121ada9189132a667ecbb5eeb31","9ecd33ad344869588ee03fad844f08224ed90062","e83399238ef09ea2aca36c0489090c9b52c7164f"],"m":1152},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1153","t":"benhur wrote:\n\nhi Benhur\n\nim still confuse about the QM entry point, why entry must be there?, there is a s/r flip or decision point at there?","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1153","p":47,"im":["7b27145e0e4439a005c2b7c111b0a17b90bc9812"],"m":1153},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1154","t":"Hi Sam, waiting for benhur's response, I can surely say that that's a nice RBD (lower edge the LL, higher edge the dotted line) that indicates strong fresh demand. And this is how the price reacted to it:\n\nHere's a step by step explanation of another QM by benhur: readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/homewo...simodo?start=50#3036","a":"Al3cs","d":"","n":"#1154","p":47,"im":[],"m":1154},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1155","t":"Thanks fou your answer\n\nYes maybe a nice RBD or fresh demand could be there, but there not just one fresh demand in the LTF, there are 1-3, fresh demand, would we trade all this demand?\n\nWhat you think?","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1155","p":47,"im":[],"m":1155},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1156","t":"Obviously was a DBR - Drop Base Rally and not RBD, excuse me for the mistake. I think that you must look HTFs (daily in this chart) for setups and go down in LTF for pinpoint the entry. So the DBR in the daily is enough. Every DBR in LTF could contain different DBR with RBR and/or RBD. This is the reason why the first HW assigned is the one inherent caps on price. You must walk on this stair step by step.","a":"Al3cs","d":"","n":"#1156","p":47,"im":[],"m":1156},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1157","t":"great QM, but im not see the supply Zone, and my question: 1. does QM valid in swap supply/demand? 2. does QM valid for FTR/FL zone?\n\nanyone may answer this one\n\nthanks\n\nIfmyante wrote: The proof of the pudding's in the eating","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1157","p":47,"im":["3b668b654b9dde065b5897e8038e373066331227"],"m":1157},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1158","t":"thanks a lot alecs, yes step by step really importance ^_^","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1158","p":47,"im":[],"m":1158},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1159","t":"Hi guys.Finally GU reached my first target!some quasimodo..\n\nIn second chart I move my stop loss too early","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1159","p":47,"im":["ae430fb96a8e9ee25b25c9abb8d97db715df6024","7e931ed17a045c92890bd377706c44d1207e4f61"],"m":1159},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1160","t":"Spotted QM levels on Gold","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1160","p":47,"im":["c182930a050f9e0e479c5e5ada422614a50c0e83","53e6c49358734988da9b5c30b80146c981989752","87a0a141825931e9c0afc813011a80e575682a6d","1736217d1b2bd50bff37eb1cada3734bd0f5854f","f52d238345bc438115b320c5a0b65c954d99c13c","3b8fdb957e8bd78e6f2a35f369fc34596358fe78","4708ff06ce52d3955943db987b425feff6f2fea0","acbb64aa67e9730a22095d69bd5ccececf6fe86e"],"m":1160},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1161","t":"","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1161","p":47,"im":["8cd0d45cf4e273fa2f0e51fb21fee46a5680492b"],"m":1161},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1162","t":"","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1162","p":47,"im":["25d27474e1c8094a37ad9d48f1dd85e83102d278"],"m":1162},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1163","t":"Hi guys!!! another quasimodo\n\nfull","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1163","p":47,"im":["7d55aae3cdcda2bb50d6d968527d934e0314ab19"],"m":1163},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1164","t":"","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1164","p":47,"im":["439bc3067d81d9e24c07671030be3fecf01c501e"],"m":1164},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1165","t":"hey staurum well done man, good start with QM look for QMs as you want to trade them where do you look for them? draw your zones in HTF and go to LTF and see the reactions the shape itself isn't rally important, try to understand the concept behind it for example in an up trend, when price approach your zone and flaged, did the LL engulf the important FL there or just engulf a less important low there? it can cause your QM fail and a Diamond create, you will get better each time you look for them and i suggest you that don't draw that lines on your QMs, they are not clear enough to investigate them keep the good work doing regards","a":"omidfxt","d":"","n":"#1165","p":47,"im":[],"m":1165},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1166","t":"omidfxt, thank you very much for your advice. please keep advising me as you find my posts later on. i need all the help i can get.\n\nRight, so Engulf significance, the engulfed significance, and i will try to keep lines off QMs. Thanks, bro","a":"staurum","d":"","n":"#1166","p":47,"im":[],"m":1166},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1167","t":"It's funny sometimes. While IF was giving his webinar on QM, the same happen and I was trading it. Easy PA","a":"mertch","d":"","n":"#1167","p":47,"im":["031847276b8f879614a63d3470e310c51318c9e7","90c398ce6e19bc1062b9c83fb1067ae907b766fa","797aa55550f360a372bdba405510e789ccd6a4c5"],"m":1167},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1168","t":"yeah, its MPL","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1168","p":47,"im":[],"m":1168},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1169","t":"What means MPL? The word is not in the abbreviation list. Maximum Pain Level? Multi Pivot Line?","a":"pazz","d":"","n":"#1169","p":47,"im":[],"m":1169},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1170","t":"yes, maximum pain level, you can find on IF 1st webinar about MPL","a":"samjardavid","d":"","n":"#1170","p":47,"im":[],"m":1170},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1171","t":"Hi all! my last quasimodo\n\nfull","a":"full","d":"","n":"#1171","p":47,"im":["f18c9a223ef6960e5acf19eb94c4617535673102"],"m":1171},{"id":"quasimodo_p47_1172","t":"full wrote: Hi all! my last quasimodo\n\nI really hope you got fill on that mate!","a":"Paraipan","d":"","n":"#1172","p":47,"im":["f18c